{title: Here Is the Bridegroom}
{subtitle: Matthew 25:1–13}
{key: F}
{tempo: 110}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [–] | [F] | [Dm] | [Bb] |
| [C] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[F]Ten young girls with their [Dm]lamps all ready
[Bb]Waiting for [C]the wedding night
[F]Five of them were fool[Dm]ish, five of them were wise
[Bb]Five brought oil to keep [C]their lamps alight
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
The [F]bridegroom was a long [Dm]time in coming
So [Bb]they all grew drowsy [C]and fell asleep
But at [F]midnight there [Dm]came a shout
And [Bb]the wise ones had [C]their oil to keep
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Here is [F]the bridegroom
Come out [Dm]to meet him
Keep your lamp [Bb]burning
[C]Keep watch, keep [F]watch
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
Give us some of your oil, our [Dm]lamps are going out
The [Bb]foolish ones cried, but the [C]wise ones said no
[F]While they were away [Dm]the bridegroom came
And [Bb]the door was shut, [C]and they had nowhere to go
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
So keep [Bb]watch
Because [C]you do not know the day or [F]the hour
Keep [Bb]watch
Because [C]you do not know the day or [F]the hour
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
Here is the bridegroom
Come out to [Dm]meet him
{end_of_verse}

{comment: Outro (instrumental)}
